    "tags": [],
    "description": {
      "value": "<p><em>You keep a quiet accounting of what should have gone wrong.</em></p><p>When you use a <strong>refraction die</strong> from Foresight Refraction to alter a roll and the result changes a <strong>failure into a success</strong>, mark one tally in your <strong>ledger</strong>.</p><ul><li>At the end of the scene, if you have at least <strong>2 tallies</strong>, you gain  before a future scene (chosen by you) as the timeline pre-cooperates with your entry.</li><li>After you receive this initiative bonus once, your ledger resets to 0 tallies.</li></ul><p>This is purely narrative bookkeeping: you’re getting credit for every disaster you quietly deflected.</p><div data-ft-per-use=\"1\" data-ft-per-use-key=\"wlForesightLedger\" style=\"margin-top:0.7rem;padding:0.55rem 0.75rem;border:1px solid #b08acc;border-radius:0.35rem;background:rgba(70,55,95,0.18);\">\n  <div style=\"font-size:0.78rem;letter-spacing:0.04em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#d4b8e8;margin-bottom:0.25rem\">⟁ Per-Use Ability — <strong>Lens Ledger</strong></div>\n  <div style=\"font-size:0.86rem;opacity:0.92;line-height:1.4\"><strong>Recovery:</strong> Tally-based &nbsp;·&nbsp; <strong>Action:</strong> Free (passive bookkeeping) &nbsp;·&nbsp; <strong>Use:</strong> Click this feature on your sheet to invoke.</div>\n  <div style=\"font-size:0.82rem;opacity:0.85;margin-top:0.3rem\">When a Foresight Refraction die converts a failure into a success, mark a tally. With 2+ tallies at scene end, gain an initiative bonus on a future scene of your choice; ledger then resets to 0.</div>\n</div>",
      "chat": ""
    },
